<title>USA: Fannie Mae ups the size of REMIC 1997-46.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae ups the size of REMIC 1997-46.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Thursday said it has increased the size of a previously issued series of Real Estate Mortgage Investment Conduit (REMIC) securities.</p>
<p>REMIC trust 1997-46, issued via Lehman Brothers, was increased to about $1.08 billion from $300 million, the agency said.  The issue is backed by 30-year 7.5 percent and 8.0 percent mortgage-backed securities and 30-year 8.0 percent Government National Mortgage Association (Ginnie Mae) certificates.</p>
<p>The issue has a settlement date of June 30, Fannie Mae said.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
